"From the source of light\nThere was something not quite bright\nPerhaps the collisions had might\nIt went straight, neither left nor right\n\nIt was the photogenic photon\nAlways ready to go in the camera\nPart of a race it could never have won\nYes, it was the photogenic photon\n\nFrom the retina of the eyes\nTo a man made to device\nEven with intention to capture\nThe photon always went inside\n\nUnable to comprehend the charge\nAlways compared itself and never won\nYes the comparison wasn't even real\nAnd yet it always saw the electron\n\nNever understood the place of itself\nIn the universe full of protons\nAlthough we study the negative particles\nBut we did acknowledged the photogenic photons\n\nPerhaps it never wanted the cameraman\nFor it always got captured inside\nPerhaps it wasn't the electrons\nThe PEE introduced was what kept it aside"